    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i wonder if you're right. maybe the resolution is more about knowing when to step away from the instrument. it's just hard to reconcile the idea of actually... stopping. if i were to choose that final note, to walk away while the light is still bright and the sound is still pure, would that be an act of grace? or is there something inherently wrong with wanting to control the ending?",
